HST Office: new Windows Installer component GUIDs, so upgrades from beta 1-4 keep every program file.

Component GUIDs are MD5(component name + "_" + PRODUCTVERSION), and PRODUCTVERSION stayed 1.0, so
beta.5 shared its component GUIDs with beta 1-4. Their HST-built .exe/.dll had FileVersion 26.8.1.1,
beta.5's have 1.0.0.500. Windows Installer then skips every shared component whose installed key file
has the higher version ("same component with higher versioned keyfile exists"), and
RemoveExistingProducts deletes beta.4's copy: soffice.bin, soffice.com and about 170 more files were
missing after the upgrade.

The new product variable COMPONENTGUIDSEED replaces PRODUCTVERSION in the GUID source. The HSTOffice
product sets it to a constant, so from beta.5 on all its components are new to beta 1-4 and the old
product's removal no longer takes files the new one needs. Keep the value unchanged while key file
versions only go up (beta.5 -> beta.6 stays a normal upgrade with shared GUIDs); change it again only
if a key file version ever has to go down. Merge-module (VC runtime) components keep their own GUIDs.
REINSTALLMODE was not used: it is package-wide and would let the MSI replace a newer system VC runtime.

License: modified upstream files keep their license (MPL-2.0).

--- a/instsetoo_native/util/openoffice.lst.in
+++ b/instsetoo_native/util/openoffice.lst.in
@@ -105,12 +105,13 @@
             CHANGETARGETDIR 1
             PATCHCODEFILE ooo_patchcodes.txt
             CODEFILENAME codes_hst.txt
             LEGACYUPGRADECODE {4B17E523-5D91-4E69-BD96-7FD81CFA81BB}
             LEGACYUPGRADEVERSIONMIN 1.0.0.0
             LEGACYUPGRADEVERSIONMAX 1.0.1.0
+            COMPONENTGUIDSEED 1.0-hst2
         }
         active          1
         compression     5
         script          setup_osl
         downloadname    HSTOffice_{productversion}_{os}_install_{languages}
         langpackdownloadname    HSTOffice_{productversion}_languagepack_{os}_install_{languages}
--- a/solenv/bin/modules/installer/windows/msiglobal.pm
+++ b/solenv/bin/modules/installer/windows/msiglobal.pm
@@ -941,7 +941,10 @@
                 # Calculating new GUID with the help of the component name.
 
                 if ( ! exists($allvariables->{'PRODUCTVERSION'}) ) { installer::exiter::exit_program("ERROR: Could not find variable \"PRODUCTVERSION\" (required value for GUID creation)!", "set_uuid_into_component_table"); }
-                my $sourcestring = $componentname . "_" . $allvariables->{'PRODUCTVERSION'};
+                # COMPONENTGUIDSEED, when set, replaces PRODUCTVERSION in the GUID source, so a product can
+                # give all its components new GUIDs without changing its version.
+                my $guidseed = $allvariables->{'COMPONENTGUIDSEED'} ? $allvariables->{'COMPONENTGUIDSEED'} : $allvariables->{'PRODUCTVERSION'};
+                my $sourcestring = $componentname . "_" . $guidseed;
                 $uuid = calculate_guid($sourcestring);
                 $counter++;
 
